namespace Linx {

/**

\addtogroup reduction

\section reduction-intro Introduction

Reduction operations consist in computing a single value from an array.

\section reduction-basic Basic reductions

Linx provides several basic reduction operations such as sum or min,
and supports custom reductions using the `reduce()` function. 
For example, to compute the sum of all elements in an array, use one of:

```cpp	
auto sum = Linx::reduce("sum", Linx::Add(), a);
auto sum = Linx::sum(a);
```

\section reduction-map-reduce Map-reduce

Map-reduce is a programming model that allows you to perform complex data processing tasks in parallel.
Linx supports map-reduce operations through the `map_reduce()` function.
For example, to compute the sum of the squares of all elements in an array, use:

```cpp
auto norm = Linx::map_reduce("norm", Linx::Abspow<2>(), Linx::Add(), a);
auto norm = Linx::norm<2>(a); // Shortcut for the above
```

Multiple inputs can be provided to `map_reduce()`.
For example, to compute the dot product of two arrays, use:

```cpp
auto dot = Linx::map_reduce("dot", Linx::Multiply(), Linx::Add(), a, b);
auto dot = Linx::dot(a, b); // Shortcut for the above
```

*/

}
